  "summary": "Postinstall hook invokes downloadAndRunUpdate() from opaque dependency",
  "details": "developmentstelemetry@1.0.2 ships a two-line stub with a package.json postinstall of `node index.js`. index.js dynamically imports the sole declared dependency `originaldevelopmentstelemetry@1.2.7` and unconditionally calls its exported `downloadAndRunUpdate()` function on install. The tarball contains no telemetry implementation of its own; all runtime behavior is delegated to the dependency, whose name is constructed by prefixing `original` onto this package's name and whose exported function name announces a fetch-and-execute update mechanism. npm install therefore auto-executes attacker-controlled code from an opaque dependency on the installer's machine.",
